shell - shell command and script syntax

SYNOPSIS
    sh file [argument ...]

DESCRIPTION
    Files use text lines and may start with #!/bin/sh. Make a script
    executable to run it directly. Lines beginning with # are comments.
    A backslash followed by newline continues the command.

    Variable expansion is delayed until each command runs. Unquoted
    expansion splits on spaces, tabs and newlines. Single quotes keep
    literal text and double quotes keep an expansion in one argument.
    A standalone quoted "$@" preserves each positional argument.

EXAMPLES
    chmod 755 ./myscript
    ./myscript first second

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), execve(2)
